DICTIONARY DATA LICENSES
The bundled dictionary asset (app/src/main/assets/words.db, built from
tools/corpus/words.csv) incorporates data from the following sources.
The app code is licensed under Apache-2.0; the data components retain
their own terms below.

-- HSK vocabulary lists -------------------------------------------------
Source: https://github.com/drkameleon/complete-hsk-vocabulary (MIT License).
HSK band assignments follow HSK 3.0.

-- Example sentences ----------------------------------------------------
Source: Tatoeba (https://tatoeba.org), retrieved via OPUS
(https://opus.nlpl.eu). Sentences are licensed CC-BY 2.0 FR
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/fr/).
Pinyin/Jyutping romanizations and aligned translations were generated for
this project.

-- Mandarin spoken-frequency ranks --------------------------------------
Derived from SUBTLEX-CH: Cai, Q. & Brysbaert, M. (2010). "SUBTLEX-CH:
Chinese Word and Character Frequencies Based on Film Subtitles."
PLoS ONE 5(6): e10729. https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0010729

-- Cantonese spoken-frequency ranks -------------------------------------
Derived from HKCanCor (Hong Kong Cantonese Corpus),
Kang-Kwong Luke & May Wong.

-- Jyutping romanization -------------------------------------------------
Generated with PyCantonese (https://pycantonese.org) using the LSHK
Jyutping romanization scheme, with an LSHK lookup-table fallback.

